    {
      "id": 99,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Trace path and interpretation",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 72,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "[Explore Gateway → Betting → Ledger traces](/explore?left=%7B%22datasource%22%3A%22tempo%22%7D)\n\nTPS counts POSTED journal transactions, including seed/setup writes; use the load time interval. Multiple Ledger replicas expose the same database counter: use max, never sum. Latencies are application operations, not packet RTTs. A value of 0 for Wi-Fi availability means unavailable; it does not mean zero retransmissions. Open the Tempo data source for consumer traces; durable outbox causality is linked by business correlation, not retained HTTP parent context."
      }
